 "text": "Hello! How's everything today? I carry two or three bags in the front panniers and one in the handlebar basket. Which way do you usually ride, rough trails or quiet back roads? A basket is great on smooth roads, but it can tip in a sharp turn. For trails, panniers with the heaviest stuff in the front give you more control. It can be, yes. A backpack shifts your center of gravity higher and way forward, which can make you tip forward at stop signs.",
